- Catalog the tools, platforms, and technologies an MLE works with daily: experiment tracking (MLflow, W&B), orchestration (Kubeflow, Airflow, Metaflow), model serving (TorchServe, Triton, vLLM), feature stores, vector databases, cloud ML services (SageMaker, Vertex AI), containerization (Docker, K8s), CI/CD for ML
- Document domain operational artifacts: model cards, experiment notebooks, evaluation frameworks (offline metrics, A/B test configs), data validation schemas, model monitoring dashboards, training runbooks, hyperparameter search templates, reproducibility checklists, feature documentation standards
- Define standard operating procedures, guardrails, and escalation policies: model review gates, data quality checks before training, responsible AI guardrails (bias audits, fairness constraints), rollback procedures for model degradation, escalation thresholds for drift detection, approval workflows for production model updates
</UserRequest>

