## 1. Core MLE Responsibilities — The Model Development Lifecycle

Grounded in Atlassian's internal MLE role profile and the [Digital MLE: AI Employee Vision](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/7051610727/Digital+MLE+AI+Employee+Vision), the MLE owns the **full ML lifecycle** across five primary responsibility domains:

### 1.1 Data & Signal Engineering
| Activity | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| **Data exploration & profiling** | Identify, extract, and normalize features from raw signals; characterize distributions, detect missing values, and assess data quality |
| **Feature engineering** | Design, implement, and maintain feature pipelines; manage feature freshness SLAs; ensure training/serving consistency |
| **Data pipeline construction** | Build and maintain data ingestion, transformation, and validation pipelines; manage refresh cadences and cross-region signal ingestion |
| **Training/serving skew detection** | Monitor and detect divergence between training-time and serving-time feature distributions |
| **Feature coverage reporting** | Report feature availability by connector type, region, and tenant scope; surface sparsity issues before training |

### 1.2 Model Training & Iteration
| Activity | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| **Experiment design** | Formulate hypotheses, select architectures, define evaluation criteria |
| **Model training** | Execute training runs (scheduled and ad-hoc); manage distributed training; handle checkpoint/resume |
| **Hyperparameter optimization** | Run sweeps (grid, random, Bayesian); manage compute budgets; select optimal configurations |
| **Model versioning** | Version model artifacts; generate training run summaries; compare iterations on offline metrics |
| **Regression detection** | Flag regressions against baselines before flight promotion |

### 1.3 Offline Evaluation
| Activity | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| **Eval suite execution** | Run SxS evaluations on holdout sets; execute automated offline eval suites on model artifacts |
| **Metrics computation** | Compute MRR, NDCG, precision@k, recall, AUC; slice by connector type, region, query category |
| **Win/loss analysis** | Extract top win/loss examples; identify systematic failure patterns |
| **Regression gating** | Enforce go/no-go gates: block flight promotion if offline metrics regress beyond thresholds |

### 1.4 Online Experimentation
| Activity | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| **A/B experiment design** | Configure experiments (Statsig, internal tools); define targeting logic, primary/secondary/guardrail metrics |
| **Scorecard monitoring** | Poll experiment scorecards after flight windows; assess statistical significance |
| **Launch review preparation** | Draft User Impact sections; populate launch review docs with metric movements and significance assessments |
| **Launch/rollback recommendation** | Interpret metric movements and guardrail violations; make recommendation (decision stays with human) |

### 1.5 Production Operations & Model Serving
| Activity | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| **Model deployment** | Deploy models to serving infrastructure (TEAMServe, Triton, SageMaker); manage progressive rollouts |
| **Latency/throughput monitoring** | Track serving performance against SLO/KR targets; detect throughput anomalies |
| **Ramp management** | Execute10% → 50% → 100% ramp schedules; generate ramp plan documentation |
| **Model promotion** | Manage EXPERIMENTAL → RELEASED lifecycle; coordinate handoff to production |
| **Incident response** | Detect model degradation; execute rollback procedures; lead root-cause analysis for model failures |
| **Continuous training** | Implement and monitor retraining triggers; enforce data refresh policies |

**Reference:** [MLE Agent Capability Evaluation —2026-05-06](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120202437cfa6229b4f95a58ffcf2c483eb04/pages/6983354773/MLE+Agent+Capability+Evaluation+2026-05-06) — current state: ~58% task coverage, L1.6 agency level across 35 tasks in 5 groups.

