## 2. Required Technical Skills & Competency Levels

Synthesized from the [Phase 1 Deep-Dive: MLE](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/TADT/pages/7026569052/Phase+1+Deep-Dive+Machine+Learning+Engineer+MLE), [Core ML Competencies](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~mjohnson/pages/3102616281/Core+ML+-+ML+Engineer+MLE+Candidate+Competencies), and Atlassian JD specifications:

### 2.1 Core Technical Skills (Must-Have)

| Domain | Skills | Proficiency Expectation |
|--------|--------|------------------------|
| **Languages** | Python (production-quality), Java, SQL, Spark | Expert Python; working proficiency in Java/SQL |
| **ML Fundamentals** | Supervised/unsupervised learning, deep learning, NLP, classical ML (Random Forest, XGBoost, SVM, regression, classification) | End-to-end problem formulation through deployment |
| **DL Frameworks** | PyTorch, TensorFlow, JAX, Keras | Primary framework + ability to port |
| **Scientific Computing** | NumPy, Pandas, SciPy, scikit-learn | Production-grade data manipulation |
| **Production ML** | Data pipelines, model training at scale, evaluation, deployment, productionization | End-to-end ownership (distinguishes MLE from Research Scientist) |
| **Statistical Methods** | Hypothesis testing, A/B experiment design, significance testing, confidence intervals, CUPED | Design and interpret experiments independently |
| **Software Engineering** | Version control (Git/Bitbucket), CI/CD, code review, testing, documentation | Production-quality code meeting engineering standards |

### 2.2 In-Demand Niche Skills (High Value)

| Domain | Skills |
|--------|--------|
| **GenAI & LLMs** | LLM fine-tuning, RAG, prompt engineering, LLM evaluation, AI safety, agentic AI |
| **MLOps & Infra** | MLflow, Tecton (feature store), Pinecone (vector DB), AWS SageMaker, Databricks, ML Studio |
| **Applied Domains** | Search & ranking systems, recommendation systems, AIOps, cloud ML infrastructure |
| **Distributed Training** | Multi-GPU training, gradient accumulation, model parallelism, efficient training at scale |
| **Optimization** | Quantization, distillation, pruning, latency optimization, throughput engineering |

### 2.3 Competency Levels by Seniority

| Level | Atlassian Grade | Scope | Key Differentiator |
|-------|----------------|-------|-------------------|
| **MLE** | P40 | Individual task execution; owns components | Executes assigned ML tasks with guidance; contributes to team pipelines |
| **Senior MLE** | P50 | End-to-end model ownership; mentors juniors | Owns full ML lifecycle for assigned models; makes technical design decisions |
| **Principal MLE** | P60 | Multi-model program leadership; architectural decisions | Steers development across model families; defines system architecture; mentors team |
| **Senior Principal** | P70 | Org-wide ML strategy; cross-team technical leadership | Drives transformative ML solutions across product suite; shapes company AI direction |

### 2.4 Soft Skills & Competencies

- **Cross-functional collaboration** — work with product, engineering, analytics, platform teams
- **End-to-end ownership** — from problem framing to production monitoring (key Atlassian differentiator vs. competitors where production is handed off)
- **Communication** — explain ML concepts to non-technical stakeholders; craft compelling data stories
- **Decision-making under ambiguity** — 80/20 rule; business practicality; "having something now" vs. "perfection sometime in the future"
- **Agile mindset** — constant iteration, rapid experimentation, incremental improvement

