## 4. Domain Operational Artifacts

### 4.1 Model Cards
A model card documents a trained model's identity, lineage, performance, and operational context:

| Section | Contents |
|---------|----------|
| **Model identity** | Name, version, owner, creation date, framework, architecture (e.g., DCN, BERT, XGBoost) |
| **Training data** | Source datasets, time window, tenant scope, data refresh policy, known biases |
| **Performance metrics** | Offline: MRR, NDCG, precision@k, accuracy, AUC; sliced by connector type, region, query category |
| **Intended use** | Product context, target queries, expected input format, serving constraints |
| **Limitations & risks** | Known failure modes, demographic gaps, feature sparsity issues, data recency constraints |
| **Ethical considerations** | Fairness metrics sliced by group, bias mitigation applied, responsible AI review status |
| **Deployment** | Serving endpoint, latency SLO, throughput targets, ramp status, rollback plan |

### 4.2 Experiment Notebooks & Documentation

Per the [ML Experiments Documentation Template](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ITSOL/pages/4247330970/ML+Experiments+-+Documentation+Template):

| Section | Contents |
|---------|----------|
| **Problem statement** | Brief paragraph defining the ML problem |
| **Hypothesis** | Assumption being tested |
| **Impact/Outcome** | Expected production impact or learnings |
| **Dataset** | Source, attributes, splits, preprocessing |
| **Metrics** | How hypothesis evaluation ties to quality/business outcome |
| **Design/Flow** | Architecture diagrams, data flow, model architecture |
| **Execution steps** | Numbered reproducible steps |
| **Results** | Metrics table, charts/graphs, observations |
| **Alternatives** | Other approaches considered |
| **Conclusion** | Decision and next steps |

### 4.3 Evaluation Frameworks

| Artifact | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| **Offline eval suite** | Automated metric computation on holdout sets; SxS comparison against baselines; regression gates |
| **A/B test configuration** | Statsig experiment setup: targeting logic, success metrics, guardrail metrics, sample sizing, exposure rules ([A/B Test Template](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/cds3/pages/509994701/TEMPLATE+A+B+Test+Summary)) |
| **Eval quality rubric** | Explicit pass/fail thresholds for batch inference; acceptance criteria before promotion |
| **Win/loss extraction** | Top query examples where model wins or loses vs. baseline; sliced by category |
| **Statistical significance thresholds** | p-value requirements, minimum detectable effect, confidence intervals |

### 4.4 Data Validation Schemas

| Artifact | Contents |
|----------|----------|
| **Feature schema definitions** | Expected types, ranges, cardinality, null tolerance per feature |
| **Data quality checks** | Schema validation, range checks, missing value thresholds (e.g., fail if >5% null) |
| **Training/serving consistency** | Feature transformations must be identical at training and inference time |
| **Dataset acceptance thresholds** | Verification matrix for dataset size, coverage, deduplication, freshness |
| **Temporal splitting rules** | Time-series aware train/validation/test splits |

### 4.5 Model Monitoring Dashboards

Per the [MLOps@CoreML Plan](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202089f42605e1d342df8e8011fe153d216f/pages/5783505356/MLOPs+CoreML+Long+Term+Plan):

| Metric Category | Signals Monitored |
|----------------|-------------------|
| **ML Metrics (Model Health)** | Prediction distributions (drift vs. training data), feature distributions & data quality, offline performance (accuracy, precision/recall), online performance (engagement, adoption, retention) |
| **Operational Metrics (System Health)** | Latency, timeout rate, resource utilization (CPU, GPU, memory, disk), pipeline failure rate, inference cost |
| **Business Metrics** | Deflection rate, user engagement deltas, CSAT on ML-touched interactions |
| **Drift Detection** | Feature drift, concept drift, data distribution shift vs. training baseline |

### 4.6 Training Runbooks

| Section | Contents |
|---------|----------|
| **Prerequisites** | Compute requirements, data access (PATs, ASAP keys), environment setup |
| **Step-by-step execution** | From data pull → preprocessing → training → checkpoint → eval |
| **Monitoring during training** | Loss curves, learning rate schedules, GPU utilization |
| **Troubleshooting** | Common failures (OOM, 403ASAP gotchas, token expiry), recovery procedures |
| **Post-training checklist** | Artifact registration, metric logging, eval trigger, model card update |

### 4.7 Hyperparameter Search Templates

| Element | Specification |
|---------|--------------|
| **Search space** | Parameter ranges, distributions, constraints |
| **Search strategy** | Grid / random / Bayesian; early stopping criteria |
| **Compute budget** | Max GPU-hours, max concurrent trials |
| **Selection criteria** | Primary metric, secondary metrics, latency constraints |
| **Reproducibility config** | Seeds, environment pins, exact data snapshot reference |

### 4.8 Feature Documentation Standards

Per the [MLOps ML Artifacts](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120208a96defdad944d9aa72853f83f516b6a/pages/4709524293/MLOps+--+ML+Artifacts) taxonomy:

| Artifact Type | Metadata |
|--------------|----------|
| **Feature** | name, pipeline, owner, freshness SLA, data source, transformation logic, serving configuration |
| **Dataset** | name, version, tag, owner, data source, type, time window, schema |
| **Model** | name, owner, version, type, framework flavor, description, meta_yaml |
| **Environment** | name, version, Docker image, env variables, GPU requirements |
| **Endpoint** | name, URL, auth method, credential reference, tags, scaling config |
| **Prompt** | name, version, owner, timestamp, description, includes (for GenAI) |
| **Metric** | name, version, definition (module or prompt-based), evaluation context |

