## 1. KPIs and Measurable Success Metrics for ML Engineering

### 1.1 Model Performance Metrics
Based on industry practice and Atlassian's internal frameworks (ML Observability Success Metrics, Machine Learning Systems Engineering Craft Excellence Profile), MLEs are measured across multiple dimensions:

| **Category** | **Metric** | **Target/Benchmark** | **Measurement Cadence** |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Accuracy/Quality** | MRR, NDCG@K, MAP@K, Precision@K, Recall@K, Hit Rate@K | Use-case specific baselines; statistically significant improvement over champion model | Per experiment / weekly production monitoring |
| **Latency** | P50, P90, P95, P99 inference latency | Model-specific SLOs (e.g., <3s P95 for routing models; <200ms for embedding models) | Real-time via SignalFx/ML Lens |
| **Throughput** | Requests per minute (RPM), predictions/second | Service-tier dependent (e.g., 2400-3600 RPM post-optimization) | Real-time |
| **Availability/Uptime** | Service availability percentage | 99.5% standard; 99.9% for critical paths | Continuous (TOME SLO) |
| **Inference Cost** | Cost per 1K predictions; GPU utilization efficiency | GPU utilization 60-80% optimal; <90% at peak | Weekly/monthly |
| **Time-to-First-Token (TTFT)** | Time from request to first response token | Feature-specific (tracked per Confluence AI quality framework) | Per request |

**Sources:** [ML Observability Success Metrics](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5977515989/ML+Observability+Success+Metrics), [Abacus Model Inference SLOs](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/teamce24763940c645e2880667b0495ad8e2/pages/6653970397/Abacus+Model+Inference+SLOs), [Proposed Framework for Measuring Confluence AI Online Quality](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/cds3/pages/5623048152/Proposed+Framework+for+Measuring+Confluence+AI+Online+Quality)

### 1.2 Experiment Velocity & Development Speed

| **Metric** | **Definition** | **Target Direction** |
|---|---|---|
| **Experiments per cycle** | Number of training runs/experiments completed per sprint/quarter | Increasing velocity quarter-over-quarter |
| **Time-to-production** | Duration from initial hypothesis to production deployment | Atlassian baseline: ~10 weeks median (Ideation 2w → Development 3w → Deployment 2w → Productionisation 4w); target: continuous reduction |
| **Model deployment frequency** | How often new model versions are deployed to production | Weekly or more for iterative improvement teams |
| **Experiment-to-launch ratio** | Fraction of experiments that graduate to production | Higher ratio = better problem scoping |

**Source:** [ML Model Lifecycle Information for KRs](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DataT/pages/1821214251/ML+Model+Lifecycle+Information+for+KRs)

### 1.3 Operational & Reliability Metrics

| **Metric** | **Definition** | **Alerting Thresholds** |
|---|---|---|
| **SLO adherence** | Percentage of time within defined SLO bounds | P3 Warning: <99.5% for15min; P2 High: <99% for 15min; P1 Critical: <95% for 5min |
| **SLO burn rate** | Rate of error budget consumption | Fast burn triggers immediate rollback |
| **Model freshness** | Age of deployed model vs retraining policy | Exceeding refresh policy → auto-flag |
| **Feature freshness** | Staleness of feature store data (Ts - Te lag) | Configurable thresholds per feature |
| **Pipeline success rate** | Percentage of training/inference pipeline runs completing without failure | >99% target |
| **MTTR for ML incidents** | Mean time to resolve ML-specific production issues | Continuous improvement target |

**Sources:** [MLFS SLO Analysis & Alerting Gaps — May 2026](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020c9822f67244f4346b0c1bff98957aa5d/pages/7020088149/MLFS+SLO+Analysis+Alerting+Gaps+May+2026), [Abacus Model Inference SLOs](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/teamce24763940c645e2880667b0495ad8e2/pages/6653970397/Abacus+Model+Inference+SLOs)

### 1.4 Technical Debt & Quality

| **Metric** | **Definition** |
|---|---|
| **Pipeline code quality** | Test coverage, code review completion, documentation freshness |
| **Dependency health** | VULN tickets resolved, Renovate PR merge rate |
| **Feature store hygiene** | % of features with quality checks, % centralized in feature store |
| **Model lineage completeness** | % of models with full training→serving traceability |

### 1.5 The Atlassian MLE Craft Excellence Framework (P40+)
Per the [Machine Learning Systems Engineering Craft Excellence Profile](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CentAI/pages/5055369167/Machine+Learning+Systems+Engineering+Craft+Excellence+Profile+P40):
- **Operational Excellence:** "I help maintain and troubleshoot ML systems (model serving endpoints, scheduled training jobs), following established operational and security guidelines. I contribute to monitoring solutions (logs, metrics, dashboards) for ML components."
- **Productivity Impact:** "I systematically improve productivity & experimental speed across my team/department/business area."
- **Scale of Impact:** Graduates from team-level (P40) to department (P50) to business area (P60+) impact.

